data: {"text":"1. My client M/s Chotanagpur Construction Co., a registered construction company having its registered office at Industrial"}

data: {"text":" Area, Ranchi, Jharkhand, is a reputed contractor engaged in various infrastructure development"}

data: {"text":" projects across the state. My client has been executing government contracts with utmost diligence and has maintained"}

data: {"text":" an unblemished record in the construction industry for over a decade."}

data: {"text":"\n\n2. My client was awarded the contract for road widening and resurfacing of Ranchi-Khunti Road (SH-4) vide Work Order No. JRCD/RAN/2025/042 dated 20.08.2025"}

data: {"text":" for a contract value of Rs. 1,85,00,000/- (Rupees One Crore Eighty-Five Lakhs only"}

data: {"text":"). The said work order was issued by your office and my client accepted"}

data: {"text":" the same and commenced the contracted work immediately thereafter in accordance"}

data: {"text":" with the terms and conditions stipulated therein.\n\n3. My client executed the contracted work with utmost dedication and professional"}

data: {"text":" competence, deploying requisite machinery, materials, and skilled workforce. All"}

data: {"text":" construction activities were carried out strictly in accordance with the technical specifications and quality parameters laid down in the contract."}

data: {"text":" My client successfully completed all contracted work by 15.01.2026, well within the stipulated time frame,"}

data: {"text":" and duly submitted the final running bills along with measurement books which were verified and authenticated by the site engineer appointed by your department"}

data: {"text":".\n\n4. Despite completion of all contracted work and submission of requisite documents, the final payment of Rs. 62,30,000/- (Rupees Sixty-Two Lakhs"}

data: {"text":" Thirty Thousand only) remains outstanding since 15.01.2026. My client has made repeated representations to your office dated 10.02.2026, 15.03.2026,"}

data: {"text":" and 25.04.2026 seeking release of the outstanding amount, but no"}

data: {"text":" positive response has been received nor has any payment been made by your office.\n\n5. The wrongful withholding of the"}

data: {"text":" legitimate dues has caused severe financial hardship to my client who has outstanding vendor liabilities that need to be discharged. The non"}

data: {"text":"-payment has adversely affected my client's working capital and business operations, causing"}

data: {"text":" irreparable loss and damage to the reputation and creditworthiness of my client in the market.\n\n6. It"}

data: {"text":" is respectfully submitted that Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908 mandates service of a"}

data: {"text":" two-month notice upon the Government or any public officer before institution of any suit against"}

data: {"text":" such Government or officer in respect of any act purporting to be done in official"}

data: {"text":" capacity. This notice is therefore being served in compliance"}

data: {"text":" with the said statutory requirement.\n\n7. My client is constrained to invoke legal remedies available"}

data: {"text":" under law including filing of a suit for recovery of the outstanding amount along with interest and damages if the"}

data: {"text":" matter is not resolved amicably within the notice period. However, my client would prefer an"}

data: {"text":" out-of-court settlement to avoid protracted litigation which would be in the interest of both parties.\n\n8. You are hereby called"}

data: {"text":" upon to release the outstanding payment of Rs. 62,30,000/- within a period of two months from the date of service of this notice,"}

data: {"text":" failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings for recovery of the said amount along with interest at the rate"}

data: {"text":" of 18% per annum from the date it became due, damages, and costs of the legal"}

data: {"text":" proceedings."}

